bug_report:
ICE on structured binding to a parameter inside the body of expansion statements outside template
This testcase ICEs on the following:

struct Point {
    int x, y;
};

void foo() {
    Point p {1, 3};
    template for (auto _ : {}) { // ok
        auto [x, y] = p;
    }
    template for (auto _ : {0}) { // ok
        auto [x, y] = p;
    }
}

void bar(Point p) {
    template for (auto _ : {}) { // ok
        auto [x, y] = p;
    }
    template for (auto _ : {0}) { // ICE
        auto [x, y] = p;
    }
}

The ICE triggers when the structured binding binds to a destructurable parameter inside the expansion statement that expands at least once (won't ICE if it is the expansion is empty).

